+---
+description: "React-free DSH Web Client runtime for non-browser product shells consuming the canonical Remote and Session object layers."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-api-client-runtime
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+`dsh-api-client-runtime` connects a Node.js product shell to an authenticated loopback DSH Web Host and assembles the same generated Remote namespaces, Connection recovery, Session list, Session objects, queue mirrors, projection stores, and history journals used by the browser Client. It loads no React or DSH Web presentation packages. Use it when an editor or desktop shell presents DSH data independently but must not reproduce DSH transport and Session synchronization behavior.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+Exchange the launch URL through the Host root route, retain the returned authority-bound cookie in the product shell's secret store, then connect:
+
+```text
+const client = await DshWebClient.connect({
+  origin: 'http://127.0.0.1:3080',
+  cookie,
+})
+
+await client.sessions.refresh()
+const sessionId = await client.sessions.create({ cwd: '/workspace' })
+client.sessions.open(sessionId)
+const binding = client.sessions.binding(sessionId)
+
+// Subscribe to binding.session and binding.eventSource.
+
+await client.dispose()
+```
+
+`client.sessions` is the canonical `ClientSessions` service face. Each `SessionFace` owns pending-submission echoes, the authoritative queue mirror, prompt and cancellation commands, projection values, and history-window paging. `SessionBinding.eventSource` publishes the contiguous durable and live event window for shell-owned transcript projection. `client.remote` exposes generated namespaces for operations not present on `SessionFace`, and `client.connection` exposes generation and recovery state.
+
+The runtime maps DSH's internal Client HTTP targets onto the supplied origin, adds the supplied cookie and matching Origin header, and creates the authenticated multiplexed Remote WebSocket through `ws`. Connection generations, logical stream reopening, baseline replacement, and Session gap repair remain owned by their existing packages. The runtime temporarily installs the transport hook only while mounting the Connection plugin and rejects concurrent graph assembly in one process; independent connected runtimes may coexist after construction.
+
