+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Delegated Host operations
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The package adds no model input. A caller may invoke already-defined Host operations through the returned `SessionFace` and `client.remote` faces.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Zero direct tokens; the invoked Host operation owns any request content.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+No direct invalidation; the invoked Host operation owns any request-prefix change.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The runtime accepts only an IPv4 loopback HTTP origin and the Web Host's authority-bound cookie authentication.
+- File upload is unavailable; text prompts, Session history, queue control, commands, and generated Remote calls remain available.
+- The package assembles one complete Client graph per call. A product shell that needs process-wide connection sharing across isolated UI runtimes must own that higher-level lifecycle.
+- The Web Client's persisted current-navigation cell is disabled automatically because Node.js has no `localStorage`; product shells own presentation selection and restore state.
+
+**Runtime invariant:** No companion is published. The package assembles existing services without retaining an independent observation of their state; its owned relation is the authenticated Node carrier exercised through HTTP/WebSocket composition coverage.
